From 177e9a05fc0bb3d4f8fd0277671aa6746054746c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:56:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 280/283] test(qwen35): harden _compose_program and guard real
 parent->child calls

Round-2 follow-up for the composite-composition slice, based on integration
4521558e6.

Robustness (fail closed instead of silently choosing):
* reject bindings for parameters the composed function does not declare;
* reject a binding whose value is not registered in the parent builder;
* reject a composed function whose parameter name is also an operation
  output (the parameter used to shadow the produced value silently);
* reject empty/non-string rename keys or values and a bare string passed
  where a returns sequence is expected.

Tests:
* five rejection tests cover those paths;
* new _compose_program spy call-graph guard asserts the parent builders
  really invoke the child composites with exact per-parent counts
  (attention_kv_cache 6, attention_subgraph 4, decoder_subgraph 2,
  gated_delta_conv_state 1, position_control 2, whole decoder graph 105)
  and exact child histograms, so reverting a reuse back to inline fails.

Equivalence is unchanged: all 59 capture_ir snapshots and every public
CoreProgram.canonical_json() stay byte-identical to the pre-refactor
baseline, including the frozen bf16 graph digest
66dd40770dbb41251f0f7ec9b15b75b604daddc95633aabc24d9e48ffff33c6d.

(cherry picked from commit f64a15c478fbe2864fb2c001f89123590b96c1bb)
